      "message": "perf(ui): cache the shown operation status on a world write revision\n\nThe tree, the status bar, the operation page and the debug panel computed\noperation::status_of (the full generation stamp) for each operation on\neach frame. They now read operation::status_shown / stale_reason_shown.\nThese keep the answer for each operation until the world write revision\nmoves.\n\n- schema::WorldRevision and app::world_rev: one flecs observer on the\n  wildcard id and one on the wildcard pair. Each OnAdd, OnSet and\n  OnRemove of each component (except the read-time memos GeoSig and\n  GeomPrintMemo) takes a fresh number from one process counter.\n- SetSetupPostScriptOptions wrote SetupDef in place (no OnSet event).\n  It now clones and sets.\n- Generation, verify, collision checks, the post, the post dialog, MCP\n  and the script API keep calling status_of, the uncached truth.\n- Row 7: op_page, state and shell read the toolpath through\n  model::with_toolpath and do not clone it.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/status_cache.rs (a build count, one test for\neach writer, undo and redo, project load, and a source scan that refuses\nan in-place component write) and by frame_cost_ops_probe (no status is\ncomputed on a still frame with 1 and 8 operations).\n\nRefs #2201\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
